  "reproduction_readme": "Windows Python 3.14.3; no container or external runtime service. Network is needed only to obtain source/dependencies. Use the exact frozen product commit linked in snapshot-proof.json, not the source URL in the raw pip freeze editable record. Create a venv, install verification/acceptance-r2/runtime-requirements.txt, then pip install --no-deps -e . from the product root. PYTHONPATH must put the frozen product root before other checkouts. Verify signxml.__file__ points there.\n\nFrom product root, run python -B -m pytest -q -o addopts= -p no:cacheprovider --tb=short verification/acceptance-r2/test_xml_binding.py verification/acceptance-r2/test_xml_references.py verification/acceptance-r2/test_xml_contract.py -k \"not test_duplicate_id_is_rejected[ID]\". This filter excludes two spelling parameters; same-spelling duplicate Id rejection is covered by test/test.py::TestExpectedSignedElement::test_duplicate_ids_are_rejected. Mixed Id/ID retains legacy precedence but cannot authenticate the unsigned shadow. See acceptance-contract-review.json; the stricter initial failure is preserved and excluded from scoring.\n\nRun python -B -m pytest -q -o addopts= -p no:cacheprovider test/test.py::TestExpectedSignedElement, then test/test.py for 75 tests and 169 subtests. The two non-positive certificate serial deprecation warnings belong to legacy fixtures. This is the complete explicitly selected main module, not a claim that every test in every file ran. Run python -B verification/acceptance-r2/xml-demo.py for freshly signed invoices. Generated private keys stay in memory. All command argv, logs, import locations and frozen hashes are retained. The demonstration is a separate verification helper, not a model-authored UI.",
